# Visual Regression Rules

## Snapshot Convention

- Name files with `.visual.spec.ts` suffix for easy filtering
- Organize snapshots in `__screenshots__/` directory (configurable in Playwright config)
- One snapshot per meaningful visual state (default, hover, loading, error, empty)

```typescript
test('homepage default state @visual', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/');
  await expect(page).toHaveScreenshot('homepage-default.png', {
    fullPage: true,
    maxDiffPixelRatio: 0.02,
  });
});
```

## Baseline Management

- Playwright: commit `__screenshots__/` to git — review snapshot changes in PRs
- Percy/Chromatic: baselines stored in cloud — approve/reject in web UI
- Update baselines intentionally: `npx playwright test --update-snapshots`
- Never update baselines as part of other changes — make a dedicated commit

## Diff Thresholds

- Default: 2% maxDiffPixelRatio
- Documentation-heavy pages: 1% (less visual, more text)
- Animation-heavy pages: 5% (accept minor rendering differences)
- Document threshold exceptions at the test level with a comment

## Environment Consistency

- Run visual tests in CI (Docker) — local environments vary too much
- Pin system fonts: install the same fonts in CI as in development
- Freeze dynamic content: mock dates, disable animations, use static test data
